<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>MINUS Benchmark Results Dashboard</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px;
            background-color: #f0f2f5;
            color: #333;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #2c3e50;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }
        .dashboard-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 30px;
            justify-content: center;
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .benchmark-card {
            background: white;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
            width: 320px;
            overflow: hidden;
            transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
            cursor: pointer;
            text-decoration: none;
            color: inherit;
        }
        .benchmark-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
            box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        .thumbnail {
            width: 100%;
            height: 200px;
/*            background-color: #e9ecef; */
            background-color: white;
            background-color: white;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
            font-size: 48px;
            color: #adb5bd;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            padding: 10px;
        }
        .thumbimg{
          witdh: 100%;
          height: 100%;
          object-fit: contain;  /* Keeps proportions, prevents cropping, and centers */
        }
        .card-content {
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .card-content h2 {
            margin: 0 0 10px 0;
            font-size: 22px;
            color: #34495e;
        }
        .card-content p {
            margin: 0;
            color: #7f8c8d;
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }
        .status {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 15px;
            padding: 5px 10px;
            background-color: #e8f5e9;
            color: #2e7d32;
            border-radius: 20px;
            font-size: 12px;
            font-weight: bold;
            background-color: #e8f5e9;
            color: #2e7d32;
        }
        .time-status {
            background-color: #eff6ff;
            color:#1d4ed8;
        }
        .reliability-status {
            background-color: #e8f5e9;
            color: #2e7d32;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>MINUS Benchmark Dashboard</h1>
    <p style="text-align:center; font-size:15px; color:#555; margin-top:-25px; margin-bottom:35px;">
        Commit: <code style="background:#e2e8f0; padding:2px 6px; border-radius:4px; color:#1a202c; font-weight:bold;">{{COMMIT_SHA_6}}</code> &bull; Last updated: <span>{{LAST_UPDATED}}</span>
    </p>

    <div style="max-width: 820px; margin: -15px auto 40px auto; text-align: center; color: #4b5563; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6;">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">
            <a href="https://github.com/rfabbri/minus" target="_blank" style="color: #2563eb; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;">MiNuS</a> is the Minimal Problem Numerical Continuation Solver.
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 0; color: #6b7280; font-size: 14px;">
            This interactive benchmark is run upon every change made to branch
            <code>master</code> of MINUS as a github action. The goal is to compare different formulations, implementation strategies, hardware, and compilers.
        </p>
        <p>
        <b>Interactivity:</b> You can click and  hover your mouse
            to see rich details of each data point (configuration, etc).
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dashboard-container">
        
        <!-- Chicago Benchmark -->
        <a href="{{CHICAGO_HREF}}" class="benchmark-card">
            <div class="thumbnail">
            <img class="thumbimg" src="figs/chicago.png" alt="Chicago trifocal problem"/>
            <!--    📷 -->
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <h2>Chicago</h2>
                <p>Trifocal problem, 14x14 system with 312 degrees of nonlinearity. Tracks time spent in paths leading to undesired roots.</p>
                <div class="status reliability-status">Reliability: {{CHICAGO_RELIABILITY}}%</div>
                <div class="status time-status">Time: {{CHICAGO_TIME}}</div>
            </div>
        </a>

        <!-- Linecircle Benchmark -->
        <a href="{{LINECIRCLE_HREF}}" class="benchmark-card">

            <div class="thumbnail">
            <img class="thumbimg" src="figs/linecircle.png" alt="Chicago trifocal problem"/>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <h2>Linecircle</h2>
                <p>Minimal problem intersection solver tracking configurations and ground-truth validation across experiments.</p>
                <div class="status reliability-status">Reliability:
                  {{LINECIRCLE_RELIABILITY}}%</div> 
                <div class="status time-status">Time: {{LINECIRCLE_TIME}}</div>
            </div>
        </a>

        <!-- Add more problem cards here as needed -->
        
    </div>

    <!-- References Section -->
    <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 55px auto 20px auto; background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 25px 30px; box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 18px; color: #1e293b; font-size: 18px; border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f5f9; padding-bottom: 10px;">References</h3>
        <ul style="list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: #334155; margin-bottom: 12px;">
                <b><a class="publink" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.09755" target="_blank" style="color: #1d4ed8; text-decoration: none;">Trifocal Relative Pose from Lines at Points</a></b>, 
                <i>IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine
                  Intelligence</i>, 2022, and <i>CVPR 2020</i> (online March 23, 2019 4:29 UTC), 
                Ricardo Fabbri, Timothy Duff, Hongyi Fan, Margaret Regan, David de Pinho (former MSc student), Elias Tsigaridas, Charles Wampler, Jonathan Hauenstein, Peter Giblin, Benjamin Kimia, Anton Leykin and Tomas Pajdla 
                (<a href="http://rfabbri.github.io/stuff/fabbri-etal-trifocal-PAMI2022-accepted-arxiv.pdf" style="color: #2563eb;">pdf</a> |  
                 <a href="https://github.com/rfabbri/minus" target="_blank" style="color: #2563eb;">code</a> | 
                 <a href="http://multiview-3d-drawing.sf.net" target="_blank" style="color: #2563eb;">datasets</a> | 
                 <a href="http://rfabbri.github.io/stuff/fabbri-kimia-etal-CVPR2020-bib.txt" style="color: #2563eb;">bib</a>)
                <div style="margin-top: 6px;">
                    <span style="display: inline-block; background-color: #dcfce7; color: #166534; font-weight: 700; font-size: 11px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #86efac; margin-right: 6px;">PAMI</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 12.5px; color: #15803d; font-weight: 500;">
                        Awarded: <a
                          href="https://www.mathinstitutes.org/highlights/algebraic-computer-vision-advances-the-3d-reconstruction-of-curves-and-surfaces-from-multiple-views"
                          target="_blank" style="color: #15803d; font-weight:
                        600; text-decoration: underline;">NSF Research
                        Institutes Highlight</a>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
